Subject: [PATCH] hw/m68k/q800: boot info screen height from the display mode

BI_MAC_VDIM took the height from graphic_height, which is 0 unless -g
is given, so a direct-boot kernel saw a screen 0 rows high.  Take it
from the mode, as the width already is.

--- a/hw/m68k/q800.c
+++ b/hw/m68k/q800.c
@@ -602,7 +602,7 @@
                   VIDEO_BASE + macfb_mode->offset);
         BOOTINFO1(param_ptr, BI_MAC_VDEPTH, macfb_mode->depth);
         BOOTINFO1(param_ptr, BI_MAC_VDIM,
-                  (graphic_height << 16) | macfb_mode->width);
+                  (macfb_mode->height << 16) | macfb_mode->width);
         BOOTINFO1(param_ptr, BI_MAC_VROW, macfb_mode->stride);
         BOOTINFO1(param_ptr, BI_MAC_SCCBASE, SCC_BASE);
 
